---
title: Billing runbook
description: Refunds and credit notes, for the finance team.
---

Internal: for the **finance** and **platform-admin** roles.

## Refund a lost or damaged parcel

{% steps %}
{% step title="Find the invoice" %}
Search by customer with `GET /invoices?customer_id=…`.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Refund" %}
Refund the parcel's line, with the reason `lost_parcel` or `damaged_parcel`. Always send a fresh `Idempotency-Key`.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Check" %}
The refund starts as `pending` and becomes `succeeded` when the payment provider confirms.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

{% api-operation spec="billing" path="/refunds" method="post" /%}

{% callout type="info" title="Generated data" %}
The Billing API spec has no examples, so the mock server makes up invoices and refunds from the schemas. Every run gives the same data.
{% /callout %}

## Goodwill credit

For a customer who had a bad week, issue a credit note instead of a refund (`POST /credit-notes`); it is used up by their next invoices.
